adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added `app/assets/javascripts/embed.js`, the code does:

```js
var comments = document.getElementById('discourse-comments'),
    iframe = document.createElement('iframe');
...
comments.appendChild(iframe);
```

There is no null-check for `comments`, so if the host page does not include an element with id `discourse-comments`, this will throw at runtime (`Cannot read property 'appendChild' of null`).

Also, the iframe URL is built via string concatenation:

```js
iframe.src = discourseUrl + "embed/best?embed_url=" + encodeURIComponent(discourseEmbedUrl);
```

If `discourseUrl` is configured without a trailing slash (e.g. `https://forum.example.com`), the resulting URL becomes `https://forum.example.comembed/best?...`, which is malformed. The code does not normalize or insert the slash.
